# Reduced TS, step 1: relax the HOST around a frozen reacting core (COMPUTATIONAL.md C8).
#
# New geometry tier: ! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) (settled 2026-09-21).
# System: the 137-atom reduced TS seed -- the verified r2SCAN-3c TS minus the
# spectator water water1 (O132 + H131 + H139). At that TS the H-bond chain is
#   O136-H135 ... O134(water2) -> O132(water1) -> O130(ketone O)
# and H135 is delivered to water2 while water1's H131 never moves.
#
# The host (120 atoms of QM2) was last relaxed around an r2SCAN-3c core, so it
# needs to settle on the B97-3c surface. The reacting core is held FIXED so the
# relaxation cannot drag the reaction coordinate:
#
#   frozen (reduced numbering, 1-based): 129-137
#     129,130        ketone C129 and O130
#     131,132,137    water2 O134, H133, H140
#     133,134,135,136  H2O2 H135, O136, O137, H138
#
# Next: NumFreq on the result (step 2), then OptTS with `inhess Read` of that
# Hessian (step 3). NOT `Calc_Hess true` in the OptTS -- its forward differences
# produced 4 spurious negatives against central-difference NumFreq's 1 and sent
# the earlier OptTS chasing scaffold modes for 350 cycles.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) opt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  # Cartesian constraints need the trailing `C`, and ORCA's constraint atom
  # indices are 0-BASED: the frozen core is 1-based 129-137 = 0-based 128:136.
  Constraints
    { C 128:136 C }
  end
  Calc_Hess true
  Recalc_Hess 50
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
